{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-96979-r4519193","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Snickerdoodles IV","sourcePageId":96979,"sourceRevision":"4519193","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T18:02:40Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Snickerdoodles%20IV&oldid=4519193","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:33.011Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Christmas recipes","Category:Dessert recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for snickerdoodles","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cream of tartar","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using superfine sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"399af64c515cd04893a46c82eb7b2d89648c478a5dc40b666df642f5d292259c","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cookie recipes\n| Servings = 36\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:Snickerdoodles.jpg|300px]]\n| Time = 60 minutes\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[:Category:Cookie recipes|Cookies]]\n\n'''Snickerdoodles''' are sugar cookies lightly dusted with [[Cookbook:cinnamon|cinnamon]]. They have a characteristically crackly surface, and can be crisp or soft, depending on preference. Some variants include nutmeg, raisins, or nuts. They are a traditional Christmas cookie in North America.\n\n''The Joy of Cooking'' claims that snickerdoodles are probably German in origin, and that the name is a corruption of the German word for \"snail noodles\" (''schneckennudeln'').\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 344 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] (2 ¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] or 24 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]]) [[Cookbook:Flour|all-purpose flour]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Cream of Tartar|cream of tartar]]\n* 300 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] (1½ cups or 9 oz) [[Cookbook:Castor sugar|superfine sugar]]\n* 110 g (½ cup or 4 oz) [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*100 g (½ cup or 4 oz) [[Cookbook:Shortening|shortening]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]] extract\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1½ tsp [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven temperatures|350°F]].\n# Mix flour, salt, baking soda, cream of tartar. Set aside.\n# [[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] butter, shortening and sugar.\n# Beat in eggs and vanilla.\n# Gradually add dry ingredients, mixing fully.\n# Roll into 1 tbsp balls.\n# Mix sugar and cinnamon.\n# Roll balls in sugar-cinnamon mixture.\n# Refrigerate for 30 minutes.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 10 minutes or until crisp and light brown.\n#Let cool completely before eating.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for snickerdoodles]]\n== Alternate recipes ==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Snickerdoodles (Boston Globe)]]\n* [[Cookbook:Snickerdoodles (Idaho Daily Statesman)]]\n* [[Cookbook:Snickerdoodles (Alternate 1)]]\n* [[Cookbook:Snickerdoodles (Alternate 2)]]\n* [[Cookbook:Snickerdoodles (Alternate 3)]]\n\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Christmas recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using superfine sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream of tartar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Snickerdoodles IV","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"36","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"344 g (2 ¾ cups or 24 oz) all-purpose flour","sourceText":"344 g (2 ¾ cups or 24 oz) all-purpose flour","amountText":"344 g (2 ¾ cups or 24 oz) all-purpose flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¼ tsp salt","sourceText":"¼ tsp salt","amountText":"¼ tsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tsp baking soda","sourceText":"1 tsp baking soda","amountText":"1 tsp baking soda","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 tsp cream of tartar","sourceText":"2 tsp cream of tartar","amountText":"2 tsp cream of tartar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"300 g (1½ cups or 9 oz) superfine sugar","sourceText":"300 g (1½ cups or 9 oz) superfine sugar","amountText":"300 g (1½ cups or 9 oz) superfine sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"110 g (½ cup or 4 oz) butter","sourceText":"110 g (½ cup or 4 oz) butter","amountText":"110 g (½ cup or 4 oz) butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"100 g (½ cup or 4 oz) shortening","sourceText":"100 g (½ cup or 4 oz) shortening","amountText":"100 g (½ cup or 4 oz) shortening","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 eggs","sourceText":"2 eggs","amountText":"2 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodB